Hi folks,

I'm well on my way to working through all the roles that this game has
to offer, having just ascended an orcish rogue.  The conducts I kept
were wishless, genocideless, and never polymorphed an object.

Found a magic lamp in minetown (preblessed too!) but decided to keep
it for lighting purposes.  Got the amulet from soko, the luckstone
from mines end, killed medusa.  I visited the castle, but didn't have
MR yet, and there were no gray dragons hiding in the closet for me.  I
went back to soko, reverse geno'd gray dragons and got myself some
lovely scales.  I then went on the quest, falling into the wrong spot
about 4 times and using a cursed ?oT to get back up a level each time.


Finished half the castle, and didn't bother with finding the wand.

In my explorations I couldn't find a drum of earthquake, so I was
unable to use my favourite tactic of wake Rodney without trudging
through his tower.  However I did find a mind flayer figurine and
realised that I could use that instead.  It took a little longer than
the drum, but still worked.

Killed Rodney, teleported down to the VS, did the ritual, teleported
down and landed outside the sanctum.  I opened the door, saw Rodney
and the priest and decided to let them fight it out.  I thought Rodney
would automatically go for whoever had the amulet, but this didn't
seem to be the case.  Have I been misinformed here?

Eventually killed the priest and two copies of Rodney, grabbed the
amulet and went to make my escape.  I then realised that I had left my
cursed gain level potion somewhere else and would have to struggle
through the graveyard.

Bugger.

Went up, killing any footrices I saw as I passed and grabbing their
corpses.  In doing so, I forgot one of my most painfully learnt rules.

"Always unweild your cockatrice before you do anything else, especially
somethings as tricky as walking."

See http://tinyurl.com/9e77l

I had a =3DoLev on so I was just zipping through the levels until I ran
over a sink.  Thankfully I was wearing a lifesaving amulet, so it was
just a nasty scare instead of a painful reinforcement of that lesson.

Needed to visit all three altars in astral to find the right one, but
with conflict and many wands of teleportation, that wasn't a huge
problem.

